get_ci_catalog_resource.query:
query GetCiCatalogResource(
            $id: CiCatalogResourceID,
            $fullPath: ID,
            $versionLimit: Int!,
            $componentLimit: Int!,
            $includeReadme: Boolean!
          ) {
            ciCatalogResource(id: $id, fullPath: $fullPath) {
              id
              name
              description
              fullPath
              icon
              starCount
              topics
              verificationLevel
              visibilityLevel
              webPath
              latestReleasedAt
              last30DayUsageCount
              versions(first: $versionLimit) {
                nodes {
                  id
                  name
                  path
                  createdAt
                  releasedAt
                  readme @include(if: $includeReadme)
                  semver { major minor patch }
                  components(first: $componentLimit) {
                    nodes {
                      id
                      name
                      description
                      includePath
                      last30DayUsageCount
                      inputs {
                        name
                        description
                        type
                        required
                        default
                        options
                        regex
                      }
                    }
                    pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
                  }
                }
                pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
              }
            }
          }

get_work_item.query:
query($path: ID!, $iid: String!) {
      namespace(fullPath: $path) {
        workItem(iid: $iid) {
          id
          iid
          title
          state
          description
          webUrl
          confidential
          author { username }
          createdAt
          closedAt
          workItemType { name }
          widgets {
            __typename
            ... on WorkItemWidgetHierarchy {
              hasChildren hasParent
              parent { id iid title webUrl workItemType { name } namespace { fullPath } }
              children { nodes { id iid title state webUrl workItemType { name } namespace { fullPath } } }
            }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetStatus { status { id name category color iconName position } }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetCustomFields {
              customFieldValues {
                __typename
                customField { id name fieldType }
                ... on WorkItemNumberFieldValue { value }
                ... on WorkItemTextFieldValue { value }
                ... on WorkItemSelectFieldValue {
                  selectedOptions { id value }
                }
              }
            }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetLabels { labels { nodes { id title color } } }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetAssignees { assignees { nodes { id username name } } }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetWeight { weight rolledUpWeight rolledUpCompletedWeight }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetHealthStatus { healthStatus }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetStartAndDueDate { startDate dueDate }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetMilestone { milestone { id title } }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetLinkedItems {
              blocked blockedByCount blockingCount
              linkedItems { nodes { linkType workItem { id iid title state webUrl workItemType { name } namespace { fullPath } } } }
            }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetTimeTracking {
              timeEstimate totalTimeSpent
            }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetDevelopment {
              willAutoCloseByMergeRequest
              relatedBranches { nodes { name } }
              relatedMergeRequests {
                nodes { iid title webUrl state sourceBranch }
              }
              closingMergeRequests {
                nodes {
                  mergeRequest { iid title webUrl state sourceBranch }
                }
              }
              featureFlags { nodes { name active } }
            }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetIteration {
              iteration { id title startDate dueDate webUrl iterationCadence { id title } }
            }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetProgress { progress }
            ... on WorkItemWidgetColor { color textColor }
          }
        }
      }
    }

list_work_items.query:
query($path: ID!, $types: [IssueType!], $state: IssuableState, $search: String, $assigneeUsernames: [String!], $labelName: [String!], $first: Int, $after: String) {
      project(fullPath: $path) {
        workItems(types: $types, state: $state, search: $search, assigneeUsernames: $assigneeUsernames, labelName: $labelName, first: $first, after: $after) {
          nodes {
            id iid title state webUrl workItemType { name }
            widgets {
              __typename
              ... on WorkItemWidgetStatus { status { id name category color } }
              ... on WorkItemWidgetLabels { labels { nodes { title } } }
              ... on WorkItemWidgetAssignees { assignees { nodes { username } } }
              ... on WorkItemWidgetWeight { weight }
              ... on WorkItemWidgetHealthStatus { healthStatus }
              ... on WorkItemWidgetStartAndDueDate { startDate dueDate }
              ... on WorkItemWidgetMilestone { milestone { id title } }
            }
          }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        }
      }
    }

create_work_item.notes:
transform `resolved_full_path` = resolveProjectOrGroupPath(project_id): decodeURIComponent(project_id), then match ^(group|project):(.+)$ — an explicit `group:` prefix is refused outright while GITLAB_ALLOWED_PROJECT_IDS (or a session scope) is non-empty; the remainder is passed through getEffectiveProjectId (GITLAB_PROJECT_ID override). With an explicit `group:` prefix it does GET /groups/{urlencoded id} and takes `full_path` (kind=group). Otherwise GET /projects/{urlencoded id} and takes `path_with_namespace` (kind=project); only if that 404s AND there was no explicit prefix AND the allowlist is empty AND the id is not all digits does it retry GET /groups/{urlencoded id} and use `full_path` (kind=group). This REST call always happens — it is NOT skipped for path-like ids. WORK_ITEM_TYPE_NAMES mapping: the lowercase tool enum is mapped through WORK_ITEM_TYPE_NAMES {issue:Issue, task:Task, incident:Incident, test_case:'Test Case', epic:Epic, key_result:'Key Result', objective:Objective, requirement:Requirement, ticket:Ticket} (unknown -> "Issue"), then spaces become underscores and the whole string is uppercased (e.g. test_case -> TEST_CASE). STEP 2 (always, GraphQL): transform `work_item_type_gid` = resolveWorkItemTypeGID(<resolved_full_path>, type ?? "issue") runs "query($path: ID!) {
      namespace(fullPath: $path) {
        workItemTypes {
          nodes {
            id
            name
          }
        }
      }
    }" with {"path": <resolved_full_path>} and picks the node whose `name` equals the mapped display name (Issue/Task/Incident/Test Case/Epic/Key Result/Objective/Requirement/Ticket — NOT uppercased here); an unknown tool type throws `Unknown work item type: <type>` and a missing node throws `Work item type '<Name>' not found in project <path>`. STEP 3 (only when labels[] or assignee_usernames[] is non-empty, GraphQL): resolveNamesToIds builds one aliased query "query($path: ID!, $usernames: [String!]!<, $l0: String!, $l1: String! ...>) {\n      <project|group>(fullPath: $path) { <l0: labels(title: $l0, includeAncestorGroups: true, first: 1) { nodes { id } } ...  or __typename when there are no labels> }\n      users(usernames: $usernames) { nodes { id username } }\n    }" with {path: <resolved_full_path>, usernames: assignee_usernames ?? [], l<i>: <label name>} — the root field is `group` when the namespace resolved as a group, else `project`. A null root throws `Namespace '<path>' not found or inaccessible`, a label with no node throws `Label '<name>' not found in namespace`, and an unmatched username throws `User '<name>' not found`. STEP 4 (only when parent_iid is supplied): transform `work_item_gid` = resolveWorkItemGID(project_id, iid): first `resolved_full_path` as above, then an extra GraphQL round trip "query($path: ID!, $iid: String!) {
      namespace(fullPath: $path) {
        workItem(iid: $iid) {
          id
        }
      }
    }" with {"path": <resolved_full_path>, "iid": String(iid)}; a missing data.namespace.workItem.id throws `Work item #<iid> not found in namespace <path>`. The value used below is that gid://gitlab/WorkItem/<n>. is run for (project_id, parent_iid) to get $parentId. STEP 5: the workItemCreate mutation. THE DOCUMENT IS ASSEMBLED AT RUNTIME — `query` below is exactly what the bundle emits when only the required args are given; each optional arg appends one variable definition to the `mutation(...)` list and one field to the `input: { ... }` list, in this order: description -> `$description: String!` + `descriptionWidget: { description: $description }`; resolved labelIds (non-empty) -> `$labelIds: [LabelID!]!` + `labelsWidget: { labelIds: $labelIds }`; weight (ONLY when type !== "incident" — incidents have no weight widget) -> `$weight: Int` + `weightWidget: { weight: $weight }`; parent_iid -> `$parentId: WorkItemID` + `hierarchyWidget: { parentId: $parentId }`; resolved userIds (non-empty) -> `$assigneeIds: [UserID!]!` + `assigneesWidget: { assigneeIds: $assigneeIds }`; health_status -> `$healthStatus: HealthStatus` + `healthStatusWidget: { healthStatus: $healthStatus }`; start_date and/or due_date -> `$startDate: Date` and/or `$dueDate: Date` + a single `startAndDueDateWidget: { startDate: $startDate, dueDate: $dueDate }` carrying only the supplied halves; milestone_id -> `$milestoneId: MilestoneID` + `milestoneWidget: { milestoneId: $milestoneId }` (a value not starting with `gid://` becomes `gid://gitlab/Milestone/<value>`); iteration_id -> `$iterationId: IterationID` + `iterationWidget: { iterationId: $iterationId }` (same gid coercion with `gid://gitlab/Iteration/<value>`); confidential -> `$confidential: Boolean` + `confidential: $confidential`. Note the namespace variable is named $projectPath but the input field is `namespacePath`. Sent through executeGraphQL (POST to <origin><prefix>/api/graphql, or GITLAB_GRAPHQL_URL; throws on a non-2xx response and on a non-empty top-level `errors` array, then returns json.data). If data.workItemCreate.errors is non-empty -> throw `Failed to create work item: <errors joined by ", ">`. The tool returns the remapped {id, iid, title, type: workItem.workItemType.name, webUrl}.

create_work_item.query:
mutation($projectPath: ID!, $title: String!, $typeId: WorkItemsTypeID!) {
    workItemCreate(input: { namespacePath: $projectPath, title: $title, workItemTypeId: $typeId }) {
      workItem {
        id
        iid
        title
        webUrl
        workItemType { name }
      }
      errors
    }
  }

update_work_item.notes:
Multi-call GraphQL tool; there is NO REST endpoint and no single document. Sequence: (1) transform `work_item_gid` = resolveWorkItemGID(project_id, iid): first `resolved_full_path` as above, then an extra GraphQL round trip "query($path: ID!, $iid: String!) {
      namespace(fullPath: $path) {
        workItem(iid: $iid) {
          id
        }
      }
    }" with {"path": <resolved_full_path>, "iid": String(iid)}; a missing data.namespace.workItem.id throws `Work item #<iid> not found in namespace <path>`. The value used below is that gid://gitlab/WorkItem/<n>. — this yields workItemGID, projectPath and namespaceKind, and is the only REST traffic (GET /projects/{project_id}, or /groups/... per the prefix/404 rules). transform `resolved_full_path` = resolveProjectOrGroupPath(project_id): decodeURIComponent(project_id), then match ^(group|project):(.+)$ — an explicit `group:` prefix is refused outright while GITLAB_ALLOWED_PROJECT_IDS (or a session scope) is non-empty; the remainder is passed through getEffectiveProjectId (GITLAB_PROJECT_ID override). With an explicit `group:` prefix it does GET /groups/{urlencoded id} and takes `full_path` (kind=group). Otherwise GET /projects/{urlencoded id} and takes `path_with_namespace` (kind=project); only if that 404s AND there was no explicit prefix AND the allowlist is empty AND the id is not all digits does it retry GET /groups/{urlencoded id} and use `full_path` (kind=group). This REST call always happens — it is NOT skipped for path-like ids. (2) When add_labels/remove_labels/assignee_usernames are supplied, one resolveNamesToIds GraphQL call resolves label titles and usernames to GIDs (query "query($path: ID!, $usernames: [String!]!<, $l<i>: String!...>) {\n      <project|group>(fullPath: $path) { <l<i>: labels(title: $l<i>, includeAncestorGroups: true, first: 1) { nodes { id } }...> }\n      users(usernames: $usernames) { nodes { id username } }\n    }"); add_labels and remove_labels are concatenated into ONE list and split back by length afterwards. (3) The main mutation, assembled at runtime. With no optional args it is exactly: "mutation($id: WorkItemID!) {
    workItemUpdate(input: { id: $id }) {
      workItem {
        id
        iid
        title
        state
        webUrl
        workItemType { name }
        widgets {
          __typename
          ... on WorkItemWidgetStatus { status { id name category color } }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetLabels { labels { nodes { title } } }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetAssignees { assignees { nodes { username } } }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetWeight { weight }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetHierarchy {
            parent { id title workItemType { name } }
          }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetHealthStatus { healthStatus }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetStartAndDueDate { startDate dueDate }
          ... on WorkItemWidgetMilestone { milestone { id title } }
        }
      }
      errors
    }
  }". Each optional arg appends one variable definition and one input field: title -> `$title: String` + `title: $title`; description -> `$description: String!` + `descriptionWidget: { description: $description }`; add_labels -> `$addLabelIds: [LabelID!]` and remove_labels -> `$removeLabelIds: [LabelID!]`, both folded into a single `labelsWidget: { addLabelIds: $addLabelIds, removeLabelIds: $removeLabelIds }`; resolved userIds (non-empty) -> `$assigneeIds: [UserID!]!` + `assigneesWidget: { assigneeIds: $assigneeIds }`; state_event -> `$stateEvent: WorkItemStateEvent` + `stateEvent: $stateEvent` with the value (state_event === "close" ? "CLOSE" : "REOPEN"); weight -> `$weight: Int` + `weightWidget: { weight: $weight }`; status -> `$status: WorkItemsStatusesStatusID` + `statusWidget: { status: $status }`; health_status -> `$healthStatus: HealthStatus` + `healthStatusWidget: { healthStatus: $healthStatus }`; start_date/due_date -> `$startDate: Date`/`$dueDate: Date` + one `startAndDueDateWidget: { ... }`; milestone_id -> `$milestoneId: MilestoneID` + `milestoneWidget: { milestoneId: $milestoneId }` (non-`gid://` values become `gid://gitlab/Milestone/<v>`); iteration_id -> `$iterationId: IterationID` + `iterationWidget: { iterationId: $iterationId }` (`gid://gitlab/Iteration/<v>`); confidential -> `$confidential: Boolean` + `confidential: $confidential`; custom_fields -> `$customFieldsWidget: [WorkItemWidgetCustomFieldValueInputType!]` + `customFieldsWidget: $customFieldsWidget` where each entry is {customFieldId: <gid://gitlab/IssuablesCustomField/<id> unless already a gid>, textValue?, numberValue?, selectedOptionIds?, dateValue?}; remove_parent -> the literal `hierarchyWidget: { parentId: null }` (no variable), else parent_iid -> `$parentId: WorkItemID` + `hierarchyWidget: { parentId: $parentId }` after resolving (parent_project_id || project_id, parent_iid) through work_item_gid. The mutation's workItem selection is verbatim: workItemUpdate(input:{...}) { workItem { id iid title state webUrl workItemType { name } widgets { __typename ... on WorkItemWidgetStatus { status { id name category color } } ... on WorkItemWidgetLabels { labels { nodes { title } } } ... on WorkItemWidgetAssignees { assignees { nodes { username } } } ... on WorkItemWidgetWeight { weight } ... on WorkItemWidgetHierarchy { parent { id title workItemType { name } } } ... on WorkItemWidgetHealthStatus { healthStatus } ... on WorkItemWidgetStartAndDueDate { startDate dueDate } ... on WorkItemWidgetMilestone { milestone { id title } } } } errors }. Non-empty errors -> throw `Failed to update work item: <joined>`. (4) children_to_add: every child is resolved to a GID via work_item_gid (child.project_id || project_id), then ONE extra mutation "mutation($id: WorkItemID!, $childrenIds: [WorkItemID!]!) {
        workItemUpdate(input: { id: $id, hierarchyWidget: { childrenIds: $childrenIds } }) {
          errors
        }
      }" with {id: <workItemGID>, childrenIds: [...]}; non-empty errors -> `Failed to add children: <joined>`. (5) children_to_remove: for EACH child, a separate mutation "mutation($id: WorkItemID!) {\n      workItemUpdate(input: { id: $id, hierarchyWidget: { parentId: null } }) {\n        workItem { id }\n        errors\n      }\n    }" run against that child's own GID (removeIssueParent); non-empty errors -> `Failed to remove parent: <joined>`. (6) linked_items_to_add: grouped by link_type (default RELATED), one mutation per group: "mutation($id: WorkItemID!, $workItemsIds: [WorkItemID!]!, $linkType: WorkItemRelatedLinkType!) {
          workItemAddLinkedItems(input: { id: $id, workItemsIds: $workItemsIds, linkType: $linkType }) {
            errors
          }
        }"; errors -> `Failed to add linked items: <joined>`. (7) linked_items_to_remove: all targets resolved, then one "mutation($id: WorkItemID!, $workItemsIds: [WorkItemID!]!) {
        workItemRemoveLinkedItems(input: { id: $id, workItemsIds: $workItemsIds }) {
          errors
        }
      }"; errors -> `Failed to remove linked items: <joined>`. (8) severity -> mutation "mutation($projectPath: ID!, $severity: IssuableSeverity!, $iid: String!) {\n      issueSetSeverity(input: { iid: $iid, severity: $severity, projectPath: $projectPath }) {\n        errors\n        issue {\n          iid\n          id\n          severity\n        }\n      }\n    }" with the ALREADY resolved projectPath (no second REST call); errors -> `Failed to set severity: <joined>`. (9) escalation_status -> "mutation($projectPath: ID!, $status: IssueEscalationStatus!, $iid: String!) {\n      issueSetEscalationStatus(input: { projectPath: $projectPath, status: $status, iid: $iid }) {\n        errors\n        issue {\n          id\n          escalationStatus\n        }\n      }\n    }"; errors -> `Failed to set escalation status: <joined>`. The tool finally returns the flattened step-3 payload plus children_added / children_removed / linked_items_added / linked_items_removed counts and, when supplied, severity and escalation_status echoed back.

