dismiss_vulnerability.notes:
Pre-flight allowlist guard (GraphQL, not REST — skipped entirely when GITLAB_ALLOWED_PROJECT_IDS is empty): first run "query getVulnerabilityProject($id: VulnerabilityID!) {
      vulnerability(id: $id) {
        project {
          id
          fullPath
        }
      }
    }" with {"id": <vulnerability_gid>}; a null data.vulnerability -> throw `Vulnerability not found: <vulnerability_id>`, and the returned project is checked exactly as in get_vulnerability (fullPath or the numeric id from gid://gitlab/Project/<n> must be in the allowlist) before any write is issued. transform `vulnerability_dismiss_input` builds the single GraphQL variable `input`: {id: toVulnerabilityGid(vulnerability_id), dismissalReason: reason.toUpperCase()} plus comment: <comment> only when a non-empty comment was supplied (falsy comments are omitted, not sent as null). toVulnerabilityGid: numeric -> `gid://gitlab/Vulnerability/<n>`, an existing gid://gitlab/Vulnerability/<n> passes through, anything else throws. reason is the lowercase tool enum uppercased, e.g. false_positive -> FALSE_POSITIVE. Sent through executeGraphQL. If data.vulnerabilityDismiss.errors is non-empty -> throw `Failed to dismiss vulnerability: <errors joined by ", ">`; if the unwrapped vulnerability is null -> throw `Vulnerability not returned after dismissal (id: <vulnerability_id>)`.

dismiss_vulnerability.query:
mutation dismissVulnerability($input: VulnerabilityDismissInput!) {
      vulnerabilityDismiss(input: $input) {
        vulnerability {
          id
          state
          dismissedAt
          dismissalReason
        }
        errors
      }
    }

